cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these experiments, please cite the companion manuscript and the
  original Bonn dataset publication listed in README.md. This entry describes
  the software accompanying the IEEE Access manuscript, not an accepted journal article.
type: software
title: "When Does Residual Learning Improve LoRa Path-Loss Prediction?"
authors:
  - family-names: Donatti
    given-names: Lorenzo Moreira
    affiliation: Federal University of Santa Maria (UFSM), Brazil
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7563-3422"
  - family-names: Marchesan
    given-names: Tiago Bandeira
    affiliation: Federal University of Santa Maria (UFSM), Brazil
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5804-9531"
  - family-names: Barriquello
    given-names: Carlos Henrique
    affiliation: Federal University of Santa Maria (UFSM), Brazil
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4454-6809"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LorenzoDonatti/LoRa-Residual-Learning"
abstract: >-
  Minimal numerical implementation accompanying the IEEE Access manuscript. Compares
  direct and residual LoRa path-loss ensembles with matched receiver information,
  grouped and buffered spatial validation, sample-count controls, and receiver
  holdouts on public Bonn measurements. Exports metrics, conditional paired
  bootstrap intervals, and distance-bin errors without plotting dependencies.
keywords:
  - LoRa
  - path loss
  - residual learning
  - radio propagation
  - spatial validation
  - machine learning
